# Production Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env` at the repository root before running the production docker-compose stack.

```env
# PostgreSQL
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<strong-random-password>

# Redis
REDIS_PASSWORD=<strong-random-password>

# Keycloak
KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<strong-random-password>
KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME=auth.yourdomain.com

# API service (injected into the api container)
DATABASE_URL=postgres://bookstore:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@postgres:5432/bookstore
REDIS_URL=redis://:${REDIS_PASSWORD}@redis:6379
KEYCLOAK_JWKS_URL=https://${KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME}/realms/bookstore/protocol/openid-connect/certs
KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=https://${KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME}/realms/bookstore

# Web app build args (baked in at build time via Vite)
VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL=https://${KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME}
VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM=bookstore
VITE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=bookstore-web
```

Generate strong passwords with:
```bash
openssl rand -base64 32
```
